(define (gf-square-free f p)
  "Square-free decomposition of a monic polynomial over GF(p) (Yun's algorithm, with the p-th-root step needed in characteristic p): pairs (g, m) with f = prod g^m, every g monic and square-free and the g pairwise coprime.

Arguments:
  F: List of exact integer.
  P: Exact integer.
Returns: List of pair (list of exact integer . exact integer).
C++: std::vector<std::pair<GfPoly, int>> datamunge::algebra::detail::gf_square_free(const GfPoly & f, long long p)"
  (%f:gf-square-free f p))

(define (berlekamp-null-space f p)
  "Basis of the Berlekamp subalgebra of a monic polynomial `f` of degree n >= 1: the polynomials v of degree < n with

`v^p\\equiv v \\pmod f`, as the null space of
`Q-I`, where row i of Q holds the coefficients of `x^{ip}\\bmod f`. For square-free
f its dimension is the number of irreducible factors. The first vector is the constant 1.

Arguments:
  F: List of exact integer.
  P: Exact integer.
Returns: List of list of exact integer.
C++: std::vector<GfPoly> datamunge::algebra::detail::berlekamp_null_space(const GfPoly & f, long long p)"
  (%f:berlekamp-null-space f p))

(define (berlekamp-factor-mod poly prime)
  "Binding-friendly wrapper around berlekamp_factor() using doubles (exact up to 2^53) for both the input polynomial and the prime, matching this module's std::size_t/fixed-width-integer-avoidance convention for SWIG-facing signatures (`std::vector<long long>` has no proven binding template in this codebase, while `std::vector<double>` already does). See berlekamp_factor() for the algorithm and preconditions.

Arguments:
  POLY: List of real.
  PRIME: Real.
Returns: List of list of real.
C++: std::vector<std::vector<double>> datamunge::algebra::berlekamp_factor_mod(const std::vector<double> & poly, double prime)"
  (%f:berlekamp-factor-mod poly prime))

(define (berlekamp-factor-count poly p)
  "Number of irreducible factors of a monic square-free polynomial over GF(p), by Berlekamp's theorem: the dimension of the null space of

`(Q-I)^{\\mathsf T}`, that is
`n-\\operatorname{rank}(Q-I)`. A square-free polynomial is irreducible exactly when it is 1.

Arguments:
  POLY: ascending coefficients (made monic and reduced mod p first). List of exact integer.
  P: a prime. Exact integer.
Returns: the number of distinct irreducible factors (for square-free input). Exact integer.
Raises: datamunge-invalid-argument (std::invalid_argument) if poly is constant.
C++: int datamunge::algebra::berlekamp_factor_count(std::vector<long long> poly, long long p)"
  (%f:berlekamp-factor-count poly p))

(define (factor-gf-p poly p)
  "Complete factorization of a polynomial over GF(p): leading coefficient times monic irreducible factors with multiplicities. The square-free decomposition separates repeated factors (taking p-th roots where the derivative vanishes), and Berlekamp's algorithm splits each square-free part.

Arguments:
  POLY: ascending coefficients; reduced mod p first. List of exact integer.
  P: a prime. Exact integer.
Returns: the leading coefficient, the factors and their multiplicities. <gf-factorization>.
Raises: datamunge-invalid-argument (std::invalid_argument) for the zero polynomial.
C++: GfFactorization datamunge::algebra::factor_gf_p(std::vector<long long> poly, long long p)"
  (%f:factor-gf-p poly p))

