(define* (dog-blobs img #:optional (num-scales 4) (sigma0 1.6000000000000001) (threshold 3.0))
  "Difference-of-Gaussians blob detection (the detector SIFT keypoints are built on, without the orientation/descriptor stages): builds `num_scales` + 1 Gaussian- blurred copies of `img` at geometrically-spaced sigma_i = `sigma0` * 2^(i / num_scales), subtracts consecutive pairs to get `num_scales` DoG images, then keeps every point that is a strict extremum (min or max) among its 26 neighbors in the resulting (x, y, scale) volume -- 8 in its own DoG layer plus 9 in each adjacent layer -- and whose |response| exceeds `threshold`. A single octave only (no image-halving between octaves like full SIFT) -- simpler, and sufficient for detecting blobs across a single order-of-magnitude size range.

Arguments:
  IMG: <image>.
  NUM-SCALES: Exact integer; default 4.
  SIGMA0: Real; default 1.6000000000000001.
  THRESHOLD: Real; default 3.0.
Returns: List of <key-point>.
C++: std::vector<KeyPoint> datamunge::cv::dog_blobs(const image::Image & img, int num_scales = 4, double sigma0 = 1.6000000000000001, double threshold = 3.0)"
  (%f:dog-blobs img num-scales sigma0 threshold))

