- https://stat.ethz.ch/R-manual/R-devel/library/stats/html/prop.test.html

Arguments:
  SUCCESSES: Integer successes in [0,n]. Exact integer.
  N: Positive independent-trial count. Exact integer.
  P: Finite null probability strictly in (0,1), default .5. Real; default 0.5.
  ALTERNATIVE: TwoSided (default), Less or Greater for true probability relative to p. Symbol (one of two-sided, less, greater); default 'two-sided.
  CORRECT: True (default) applies the capped half-count correction to z. Boolean; default #t.
  CONF-LEVEL: Finite confidence level in (0,1), default .95. Real; default 0.94999999999999996.
Returns: statistic=z^2, parameter1=1, estimate1=successes/n, p_value and uncorrected Wilson confidence bounds. <hypothesis-test-result>.
Raises: datamunge-invalid-argument (std::invalid_argument) Invalid counts, null probability, alternative or confidence level.
C++: HypothesisTestResult datamunge::stats::proportion_test_one_sample(std::size_t successes, std::size_t n, double p = 0.5, Alternative alternative = TwoSided, bool correct = true, double conf_level = 0.94999999999999996)

