(define* (wilcoxon-signed-rank-test x #:optional (mu 0.0) (alternative 'two-sided))
  "Normal-approximation Wilcoxon signed-rank test with tie/continuity corrections.

Tests symmetry of x-mu about zero under independent observations, not an arbitrary-population
mean or median null. For paired data pass aligned differences. Exact-zero differences are
removed; absolute differences receive average ranks. Always uses a normal approximation, even
for small tie-free samples; no exact option or CI. O(n log n) work/O(n) storage; input
unchanged, no shared state.

Example:
    const auto w=dm::stats::wilcoxon_signed_rank_test({1,2,3,4});
    std::print(\"{:.0f}\\n\",w.statistic); // 10

References:
- https://stat.ethz.ch/R-manual/R-devel/library/stats/html/wilcox.test.html

Arguments:
  X: Finite values; at least one nonzero difference from mu must remain. List of real.
  MU: Finite symmetry centre, default zero. Real; default 0.0.
  ALTERNATIVE: TwoSided (default), Less or Greater for the signed location shift. Symbol (one of two-sided, less, greater); default 'two-sided.
Returns: statistic=positive rank sum V, estimate1=mu (not an estimated pseudomedian), approximate p_value; no CI. <hypothesis-test-result>.
Raises: datamunge-invalid-argument (std::invalid_argument) Nonfinite input/mu, invalid alternative, no nonzero differences or zero rank variance.
C++: HypothesisTestResult datamunge::stats::wilcoxon_signed_rank_test(const std::vector<double> & x, double mu = 0.0, Alternative alternative = TwoSided)

See also: HypothesisTestResult"
  (%f:wilcoxon-signed-rank-test x mu alternative))

(define* (wilcoxon-rank-sum-test x y #:optional (alternative 'two-sided))
  "Tie/continuity-corrected Mann-Whitney U test using a normal approximation.

Pools ranks, giving average ranks to ties, and reports U for the first sample. Its identical-
distribution null requires independent exchangeable samples. A common-shape shift model
supports a location interpretation; equal medians alone is insufficient. U/(n_x*n_y) estimates
P(X>Y)+P(X=Y)/2, not a mean difference. Approximation is used at every size. O(N log N)
work/O(N) storage, inputs unchanged, no shared state.

Example:
    const auto w=dm::stats::wilcoxon_rank_sum_test({1,2,3},{4,5,6});
    std::print(\"{:.0f}\\n\",w.statistic); // 0

References:
- https://stat.ethz.ch/R-manual/R-devel/library/stats/html/wilcox.test.html

Arguments:
  X: Nonempty finite first sample. List of real.
  Y: Nonempty finite independent second sample. List of real.
  ALTERNATIVE: TwoSided (default), Less or Greater for first-versus-second stochastic location. Symbol (one of two-sided, less, greater); default 'two-sided.
Returns: statistic=U=rank_sum(x)-n_x(n_x+1)/2 and approximate p_value; no CI or location estimate. <hypothesis-test-result>.
Raises: datamunge-invalid-argument (std::invalid_argument) Empty/nonfinite samples, invalid alternative or zero rank variance (all pooled observations tied).
C++: HypothesisTestResult datamunge::stats::wilcoxon_rank_sum_test(const std::vector<double> & x, const std::vector<double> & y, Alternative alternative = TwoSided)

See also: HypothesisTestResult"
  (%f:wilcoxon-rank-sum-test x y alternative))

