    const auto r=dm::fem::FEM1D::solve(dm::fem::make_uniform_mesh1d(0,1,2),{1},{0},source,{},{});
    std::print(\"{}\\n\",r.value_at(1)); // 0.125

References:
- https://mfem.org/fem_weak_form/ ; native interval P1 and quadrature choices as FEM1D.

Arguments:
  MESH: Borrowed mesh with at least two finite strictly increasing nodes. <mesh1-d>.
  P: Borrowed diffusion coefficient: length1 or one per element. List of real.
  Q: Borrowed reaction coefficient: length1 or one per element. List of real.
  F: Borrowed spatial source; evaluate() may have caller-owned side effects. <scalar-field1-d>.
  LEFT: Left endpoint condition, with outward normal -1. <boundary-condition1-d>.
  RIGHT: Right endpoint condition, with outward normal +1. <boundary-condition1-d>.
Returns: Owned original nodes and computed nodal values. <fem1-d-result>.
Raises: datamunge-invalid-argument (std::invalid_argument) If p/q are empty or have the wrong lengths.
Raises: datamunge-memory-error (std::bad_alloc) If assembly/result storage cannot be allocated; callback exceptions propagate.
