- G. H. Golub, M. Heath and G. Wahba (1979). Generalized cross-validation as a
  method for choosing a good ridge parameter. https://doi.org/10.1080/00401706.1979.10489751

`n_basis` B-splines of the given `degree` with equally spaced knots over the range of `x`, penalized with smoothing parameter `lambda` on differences of order `penalty_order`.

See the class example for a degree-one, order-two fit.

Cubic basis on the given knot locations; boundary knots are the smallest/largest of `knots` and `x`. The difference penalty assumes roughly even spacing. λ chosen by GCV. Uses the same bounded GCV search as the basis-count constructor.

Example:
    const dm::Vector<> x=dm::seql(0,1,30);
    const dm::PSR fit(x,dm::sin(6*x),dm::seql(0,1,8));
    std::print(\"{}\\n\",fit.basis_size()); // 10

Basis on the given knot locations with a fixed smoothing parameter `lambda`. Outer spacings are continued past the domain, without repeated boundary knots. The penalty acts on coefficient index and does not correct for unequal knot spacing.

